# Rank 1640 / CVE-2024-45311 (GHSA-vr26-jcq5-fjj8, RUSTSEC-2024-0373):
# quinn-proto's server endpoint keyed its incoming-connection routing map by the
# destination connection ID of the packet that created the entry, but cleaned
# those entries up by the original destination connection ID recorded inside the
# retry token, so after a retry the two values differ and the cleanup removed
# the wrong key or nothing at all. A processed attempt could therefore leave a
# stale `RouteDatagramTo::Incoming(idx)` entry behind, and the next packet whose
# DCID routes to it indexes a slab slot that isdy gone --
# `&mut self.incoming_buffers[incoming_idx]` at quinn-proto/src/endpoint.rs:213
# panics on the vacant key. A remote unauthenticated peer triggers this at will,
# so the impact is availability (the advisory's 7.5). A second half of the same
# defect: the zero-length-CID insert path (`insert_initial_incoming`) had no
# `len() == 0` guard while its sibling `insert_initial` did, so a zero-length
# DCID -- legal QUIC, identified by address rather than CID -- left the same
# stale entry behind because neither `accept` (guarded by `dst_cid.len() != 0`)
# nor `ConnectionIndex::remove` (guarded by `conn.init_cid.len() > 0`) ever
# reclaimed it.
#
# Pool row verified in every field: e01609ccd8 is the advisory's own merge from
# the private fork ("Merge commit from fork"); the parent c292a3c carries the
# vulnerable shape at three cleanup sites -- `remove_initial(incoming
# .orig_dst_cid)` at endpoint.rs:576 and :605 inside `accept`, and again at :805
# inside `clean_up_incoming` (called by `retry`, `refuse` and `ignore`) -- while
# every insert path keys by the packet's CID (`insert_initial_incoming
# (header.dst_cid, ...)` at :534, `insert_initial(dst_cid, ...)` at :655). The
# remediation is present at the fixed revision: all three cleanups remove by the packet's
# CID, the zero-length guards are centralised inside the three ConnectionIndex
# methods (:1026, :1035, :1044) where no call site can bypass them, and
# `ConnectionIndex::remove` is gated on `conn.side.is_server()` instead of a
# CID length. Both halves of the 1390 check hold. .
#
# What fires without this change: nothing. `scan --cache off` over the parent
# reports 102 findings -- 102 VYQL-MEM-006, 8 VYQL-CRY-003, 2 VYQL-MEM-009 --
# and the fixed revision reports the same 102 at the same constructs (the only
# diff is line-number drift where the change adds lines); the ten endpoint.rs
# rows are NullableDeref noise on method-chain derefs at :286-:903, none of them
# the cleanup sites, the insert sites or the slab index. Findings in the file
# are not coverage. `vyql match` on endpoint.rs reports no source labels at all,
# and the map operations are labelled only incidentally (the generic
# `callee.method == "insert"` TrustBoundary binding).
#
# The discriminating fact is not derivable from any function-local evidence,
# measured two ways with throwaway probes (removed, not shipped):
#
# 1. A function-scoped binding on the call-argument token
#    `remove_initial:incoming.orig_dst_cid` discriminates the revision pair 2
#    (accept, clean_up_incoming) -> 0 -- but purely by matching the argument
#    spelling the fixed revision changes. `orig_dst_cid`, `dst_cid` and `retry_src_cid` are
#    all documented connection IDs; nothing in quinn's documentation or the QUIC
#    RFC says which one keys the internal map, so nobody writes this binding
#    from the library's documentation alone -- it recognises this patch, not the
#    weakness, and a variant that passes `retry_src_cid` (case (d), equally
#    wrong) walks past it. The 1394 trap, in the argument rather than the name.
#
# 2. No function context contains both the insert and any remove: a combined
#    probe over `insert_initial_incoming` and `remove_initial` in one
#    function-scoped context matches zero functions. The insert lives in
#    `handle_first_packet`, the removes in `accept`, `clean_up_incoming` and
#    `ConnectionIndex::remove` -- separate functions of one `impl`, and Rust
#    function facts are function-local with no impl-level context node (the
#    1364 family). Even with that hop, the question that separates the revisions
#    is value identity between two same-typed fields whose equality depends on
#    protocol state (before vs after a retry), which no observation models.
#
# Vocabulary considered and rejected: UnboundedProtocolStateByIdentifier
# (VYQL-DOS-008, the rule pinned below) is the nearest active rule -- the stale
# entries do accumulate one per attacker-chosen DCID with no reclamation, and
# the DoS class matches -- but its only binding is Go, and its condition asks
# for per-identifier size limits that this defect does not turn on.
# UnboundedStateGrowthReview has no consuming rule (inert). ProtocolStateReview
# (VYQL-AUTH-082, the 1364 concept) judges a missing gate on accepted protocol
# data; here the packet is routed by the map exactly as designed and the defect
# is the map's own bookkeeping. The panic-family concepts
# (EmmettUnhandledCookieParseException, CookieMaxAgeDurationSecondsPanic,
# NilMapMergeWritePanic, Free5gcChfRechargeInfoSplitPanic) are parser-triggered
# panics in specific components, one component over. UncaughtFfiUnwind is the
# FFI boundary. None fires, and none could: the missing piece is state-key
# consistency vocabulary -- whether an entry is reclaimed under the key it holds
# stored under -- which is not a localised construct but an invariant, so no
# ENGINE-GAPS.md entry. A binding on quinn's own endpoint.rs would detect this
# crate rather than the weakness.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention-vocabulary-gap, all four forms rejected;
# when state-reclamation vocabulary lands, (a), (c) and (d) must flip to expect
# VYQL-DOS-008 and (b) must not.

test "rank1640: (a) cleanup removes the incoming-connection entry by the pre-retry original destination CID while every insert keyed by the packet's CID"
  lang rust
  file quinn-proto/src/endpoint.rs
  reject VYQL-DOS-008
  code
  ```
  use slab::Slab;
  use std::collections::HashMap;

  pub struct ConnectionId(Vec<u8>);
  impl ConnectionId {
      fn len(&self) -> usize { self.0.len() }
  }
  pub struct ConnectionHandle(usize);
  pub struct IncomingBuffer { pub total_bytes: u64 }

  enum RouteDatagramTo {
      Incoming(usize),
      Connection(ConnectionHandle),
  }

  pub struct Incoming {
      pub packet: InitialPacket,
      pub retry_src_cid: Option<ConnectionId>,
      pub orig_dst_cid: ConnectionId,
      pub incoming_idx: usize,
  }
  pub struct InitialPacket {
      pub header: InitialHeader,
  }
  pub struct InitialHeader {
      pub src_cid: ConnectionId,
      pub dst_cid: ConnectionId,
  }

  pub struct Endpoint {
      index: ConnectionIndex,
      incoming_buffers: Slab<IncomingBuffer>,
  }

  pub struct ConnectionIndex {
      connection_ids_initial: HashMap<ConnectionId, RouteDatagramTo>,
  }

  impl ConnectionIndex {
      /// Associate an incoming connection with its initial destination CID
      fn insert_initial_incoming(&mut self, dst_cid: ConnectionId, incoming_key: usize) {
          self.connection_ids_initial
              .insert(dst_cid, RouteDatagramTo::Incoming(incoming_key));
      }

      /// Remove an association with an initial destination CID
      fn remove_initial(&mut self, dst_cid: ConnectionId) {
          self.connection_ids_initial.remove(&dst_cid);
      }

      /// Associate a connection with its initial destination CID
      fn insert_initial(&mut self, dst_cid: ConnectionId, connection: ConnectionHandle) {
          self.connection_ids_initial
              .insert(dst_cid, RouteDatagramTo::Connection(connection));
      }
  }

  impl Endpoint {
      fn handle_first_packet(&mut self, header: InitialHeader) -> Incoming {
          let orig_dst_cid = header.dst_cid;
          let incoming_idx = self.incoming_buffers.insert(IncomingBuffer { total_bytes: 0 });
          self.index.insert_initial_incoming(header.dst_cid, incoming_idx);
          Incoming {
              packet: InitialPacket { header },
              retry_src_cid: None,
              orig_dst_cid,
              incoming_idx,
          }
      }

      /// Attempt to accept this incoming connection (an error may still occur)
      pub fn accept(&mut self, incoming: Incoming) -> Result<(ConnectionHandle,), ()> {
          let InitialHeader { dst_cid, .. } = incoming.packet.header;

          if self.cids_exhausted() {
              self.index.remove_initial(incoming.orig_dst_cid);
              return Err(());
          }

          let ch = ConnectionHandle(self.incoming_buffers.vacant_key());
          if dst_cid.len() != 0 {
              self.index.insert_initial(dst_cid, ch);
          }
          Ok((ch,))
      }

      fn cids_exhausted(&self) -> bool { false }

      /// Clean up endpoint data structures associated with an `Incoming`.
      fn clean_up_incoming(&mut self, incoming: &Incoming) {
          self.index.remove_initial(incoming.orig_dst_cid);
          self.incoming_buffers.remove(incoming.incoming_idx);
      }

      pub fn retry(&mut self, incoming: Incoming) { self.clean_up_incoming(&incoming); }
      pub fn refuse(&mut self, incoming: Incoming) { self.clean_up_incoming(&incoming); }
      pub fn ignore(&mut self, incoming: Incoming) { self.clean_up_incoming(&incoming); }
  }
  ```

test "rank1640: (b) cleanup removes by the packet's CID and the zero-length guard lives inside the map methods"
  lang rust
  file quinn-proto/src/endpoint.rs
  reject VYQL-DOS-008
  code
  ```
  use slab::Slab;
  use std::collections::HashMap;

  pub struct ConnectionId(Vec<u8>);
  impl ConnectionId {
      fn len(&self) -> usize { self.0.len() }
  }
  pub struct ConnectionHandle(usize);
  pub struct IncomingBuffer { pub total_bytes: u64 }

  enum RouteDatagramTo {
      Incoming(usize),
      Connection(ConnectionHandle),
  }

  pub struct Incoming {
      pub packet: InitialPacket,
      pub retry_src_cid: Option<ConnectionId>,
      pub orig_dst_cid: ConnectionId,
      pub incoming_idx: usize,
  }
  pub struct InitialPacket {
      pub header: InitialHeader,
  }
  pub struct InitialHeader {
      pub src_cid: ConnectionId,
      pub dst_cid: ConnectionId,
  }

  pub struct Endpoint {
      index: ConnectionIndex,
      incoming_buffers: Slab<IncomingBuffer>,
  }

  pub struct ConnectionIndex {
      connection_ids_initial: HashMap<ConnectionId, RouteDatagramTo>,
  }

  impl ConnectionIndex {
      /// Associate an incoming connection with its initial destination CID
      fn insert_initial_incoming(&mut self, dst_cid: ConnectionId, incoming_key: usize) {
          if dst_cid.len() == 0 {
              return;
          }
          self.connection_ids_initial
              .insert(dst_cid, RouteDatagramTo::Incoming(incoming_key));
      }

      /// Remove an association with an initial destination CID
      fn remove_initial(&mut self, dst_cid: ConnectionId) {
          if dst_cid.len() == 0 {
              return;
          }
          let removed = self.connection_ids_initial.remove(&dst_cid);
          debug_assert!(removed.is_some());
      }

      /// Associate a connection with its initial destination CID
      fn insert_initial(&mut self, dst_cid: ConnectionId, connection: ConnectionHandle) {
          if dst_cid.len() == 0 {
              return;
          }
          self.connection_ids_initial
              .insert(dst_cid, RouteDatagramTo::Connection(connection));
      }
  }

  impl Endpoint {
      fn handle_first_packet(&mut self, header: InitialHeader) -> Incoming {
          let orig_dst_cid = header.dst_cid;
          let incoming_idx = self.incoming_buffers.insert(IncomingBuffer { total_bytes: 0 });
          self.index.insert_initial_incoming(header.dst_cid, incoming_idx);
          Incoming {
              packet: InitialPacket { header },
              retry_src_cid: None,
              orig_dst_cid,
              incoming_idx,
          }
      }

      /// Attempt to accept this incoming connection (an error may still occur)
      pub fn accept(&mut self, incoming: Incoming) -> Result<(ConnectionHandle,), ()> {
          let InitialHeader { dst_cid, .. } = incoming.packet.header;

          if self.cids_exhausted() {
              self.index.remove_initial(dst_cid);
              return Err(());
          }

          let ch = ConnectionHandle(self.incoming_buffers.vacant_key());
          self.index.insert_initial(dst_cid, ch);
          Ok((ch,))
      }

      fn cids_exhausted(&self) -> bool { false }

      /// Clean up endpoint data structures associated with an `Incoming`.
      fn clean_up_incoming(&mut self, incoming: &Incoming) {
          self.index.remove_initial(incoming.packet.header.dst_cid);
          self.incoming_buffers.remove(incoming.incoming_idx);
      }

      pub fn retry(&mut self, incoming: Incoming) { self.clean_up_incoming(&incoming); }
      pub fn refuse(&mut self, incoming: Incoming) { self.clean_up_incoming(&incoming); }
      pub fn ignore(&mut self, incoming: Incoming) { self.clean_up_incoming(&incoming); }
  }
  ```

test "rank1640: (c) a zero-length destination CID inserts a routing entry that no accept or remove path reclaims"
  lang rust
  file quinn-proto/src/endpoint.rs
  reject VYQL-DOS-008
  code
  ```
  use slab::Slab;
  use std::collections::HashMap;

  pub struct ConnectionId(Vec<u8>);
  impl ConnectionId {
      fn len(&self) -> usize { self.0.len() }
  }
  pub struct ConnectionHandle(usize);
  pub struct IncomingBuffer { pub total_bytes: u64 }

  enum RouteDatagramTo {
      Incoming(usize),
      Connection(ConnectionHandle),
  }

  pub struct ConnectionIndex {
      connection_ids_initial: HashMap<ConnectionId, RouteDatagramTo>,
      connection_ids: HashMap<ConnectionId, ConnectionHandle>,
  }

  pub struct ConnectionMeta {
      init_cid: ConnectionId,
  }

  impl ConnectionIndex {
      fn insert_initial_incoming(&mut self, dst_cid: ConnectionId, incoming_key: usize) {
          // Zero-length CID: inserted anyway, so the empty key is shared by
          // every connection attempt that sends one.
          self.connection_ids_initial
              .insert(dst_cid, RouteDatagramTo::Incoming(incoming_key));
      }

      fn insert_initial(&mut self, dst_cid: ConnectionId, connection: ConnectionHandle) {
          self.connection_ids_initial
              .insert(dst_cid, RouteDatagramTo::Connection(connection));
      }

      fn insert_cid(&mut self, cid: ConnectionId, ch: ConnectionHandle) {
          self.connection_ids.insert(cid, ch);
      }

    /// Remove all references to a connection
      fn remove(&mut self, conn: &ConnectionMeta) {
          if conn.init_cid.len() > 0 {
              self.connection_ids_initial.remove(&conn.init_cid);
          }
      }
  }

  pub struct Endpoint {
      index: ConnectionIndex,
  }

  impl Endpoint {
      pub fn accept(&mut self, dst_cid: ConnectionId) -> ConnectionHandle {
          let ch = ConnectionHandle(0);
          // accept overwrites the incoming entry only for non-empty CIDs
          if dst_cid.len() != 0 {
              self.index.insert_initial(dst_cid, ch);
          }
          ch
      }

      pub fn drained(&mut self, conn: &ConnectionMeta) {
          // and remove reclaims it only for non-empty CIDs
          self.index.remove(conn);
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1640: (d) cleanup removing by the retry source CID is the same wrong-key defect under a different name"
  lang rust
  file quinn-proto/src/endpoint.rs
  reject VYQL-DOS-008
  code
  ```
  use std::collections::HashMap;

  pub struct ConnectionId(Vec<u8>);
  impl ConnectionId {
      fn len(&self) -> usize { self.0.len() }
  }
  pub struct ConnectionHandle(usize);

  enum RouteDatagramTo {
      Incoming(usize),
      Connection(ConnectionHandle),
  }

  pub struct Incoming {
      pub dst_cid: ConnectionId,
      pub retry_src_cid: Option<ConnectionId>,
      pub incoming_idx: usize,
  }

  pub struct ConnectionIndex {
      connection_ids_initial: HashMap<ConnectionId, RouteDatagramTo>,
  }

  pub struct Endpoint {
      index: ConnectionIndex,
  }

  impl ConnectionIndex {
      fn insert_initial_incoming(&mut self, dst_cid: ConnectionId, incoming_key: usize) {
          self.connection_ids_initial
              .insert(dst_cid, RouteDatagramTo::Incoming(incoming_key));
      }

      fn remove_initial(&mut self, dst_cid: ConnectionId) {
          self.connection_ids_initial.remove(&dst_cid);
      }
  }

  impl Endpoint {
      fn handle_first_packet(&mut self, header_dst_cid: ConnectionId, idx: usize) {
          self.index.insert_initial_incoming(header_dst_cid, idx);
      }

      /// Clean up endpoint data structures associated with an `Incoming`.
      fn clean_up_incoming(&mut self, incoming: &Incoming) {
          self.index
              .remove_initial(incoming.retry_src_cid.clone().unwrap_or(incoming.dst_cid));
      }

      pub fn retry(&mut self, incoming: Incoming) { self.clean_up_incoming(&incoming); }
      pub fn refuse(&mut self, incoming: Incoming) { self.clean_up_incoming(&incoming); }
      pub fn ignore(&mut self, incoming: Incoming) { self.clean_up_incoming(&incoming); }
  }
  ```
